<!--
  The themed-icon layer. When the launcher is set to themed icons it draws
  THIS, tinted to the wallpaper, directly on its own circle — so the icon is
  the five rows and nothing else.

  Without this layer Android has only the legacy PNG to work from, and what it
  does with one is put the whole square on a white disc inside the launcher's
  circle: a white blob with the board shrunk inside it.

  One flat colour on purpose: the system replaces it, so a gradient here would
  simply be thrown away.
-->
